I'll start by locating the existing Messenger components and the solopreneur integration points.## 1. Review & Understand the Task

- The **Messages** section of `/solopreneur` currently renders a **mock thread** (`SolopreneurMessages.vue`): fake seeded messages, fake "AI typing" reply engine (`sendMessage` / `pickReply` in `useSolopreneur.js`).
- Goal: that section must **open the existing "Messenger"**, i.e. reuse the components that already implement it — not reimplement chat.
- Acceptance criteria: clicking **Messages** in the solopreneur rail renders the real Messenger (channel rail + conversation + composer), with the section filling the content area, and no duplicate chat implementation left in the solopreneur module.

## 2. Information gathered

- `src/views/MessengerView.vue` — the Messenger screen. Composes `MessengerChannelList` (channel rail) + `ChatView` (conversation) + `MessengerGroupInfo`; emits `settings` / `account-settings`. It is a full-height screen (`flex h-full w-full`).
- `src/config/apps.js` → `APPS.messenger` (single mode pushes `/:projectName/messenger`, desktop mode opens a panel); component registered in `appComponentsMap.js` as `'messenger': MessengerView`.
- `src/components/solopreneur/SolopreneurView.vue` — module host; content area is `<main class="... overflow-y-auto px-4 … py-6">`, i.e. a scrolling card column. A full-height app cannot live there without a per-module layout rule.
- `src/components/solopreneur/SolopreneurMessages.vue` — current mock thread (to be replaced).
- `src/components/solopreneur/useSolopreneur.js` — holds the mock `messages` seed / `sendMessage` / `ui.typing`, used **only** by that component.
- `SolopreneurSidebar.vue` ("Messages" nav item) and `SolopreneurModal.vue` (`messageTeam()` → `goModule('messages')`) need **no change**: they keep pointing at the `messages` module.
- Verified the mock chat state is not consumed by any other solopreneur module (summary, updates, sprints, wallet, account, topbar, modal, sidebar, calendar).

## 3. Proposal

1. **`SolopreneurMessages.vue` becomes a thin host** for the existing `MessengerView` (so `SolopreneurView`'s module map stays untouched), covering the whole content box edge-to-edge, and mapping `account-settings` → `goModule('account')`.
2. **`SolopreneurView.vue` gains a "fill" layout tier**: modules listed in `FILL_MODULES` (`messages`) get `overflow-hidden` and no page padding/scroll, so the Messenger can use `h-full`; every other module keeps the current padded, scrollable card column. This is required because the Messenger is a full screen, not a dashboard card.
3. **Not done (needs your OK)**: removing the now-unused mock chat state in `useSolopreneur.js` (`messages` seed, `sendMessage`, `pickReply`, `ui.typing`, and its unused `ms.*` i18n keys). It is dead code after this change but touching that 600-line file is not required for the feature; say the word and I'll strip it.

## 4. Changes summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/solopreneur/SolopreneurMessages.vue` | Rewritten: renders the existing `MessengerView` full-height instead of the mock thread; maps `account-settings` to the Account module. |
| `src/views/SolopreneurView.vue` | Adds `FILL_MODULES` + `fillsContent` and applies a padding/scroll-free `<main>` for those modules. |

## 5. The Changes

